    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score of 81.88. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a premier matchup against L\u00f3pez, R, combined with a significant park factor boost and his established presence in the three-hole, making him a cornerstone for production. Following closely, **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) provide exceptional utility. **Drake Baldwin** leverages an elite leadoff spot and a favorable park, while **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Junk. Both are prioritized to maximize our daily R and RBI output while navigating the volatility of their respective matchups.\n\nTactically, we are banking on aggressive volume from our top-tier hitters, but we must account for the specific situational dynamics. **Heliot Ramos** (55.10) sits in a slightly lower efficiency tier, partially due to a drag from his opponent\u2019s ability to suppress stolen bases, keeping our SB strategy tempered despite the wind-out benefit. The most difficult decision of the day involved **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who barely missed the starting nine with a 47.58 score. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** brings valuable speed, his efficiency was suppressed by a poor platoon matchup against Drake, which tipped the optimizer toward the higher-ceiling profiles of **Dominic Smith** and **Andy Pages**\u2014both of whom cleared the 60-point threshold for mandatory inclusion.\n\nRisks remain on the horizon: while we are largely avoiding elite arms, the SP_xERA for many of our opponents hovers in the mid-4.00s, suggesting a high-variance day for our sluggers. We are keeping a close eye on the weather conditions impacting **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, whose 63.39 score is slightly suppressed by a \"wind-in\" factor at his venue, despite a favorable order position. With **Brayan Rocchio** falling well below our 40-point floor due to a brutal matchup against Rasmussen, we are comfortable with today\u2019s construction, relying on the high-efficiency trio of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Jackson Merrill** to carry the offensive load.",
